    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d437">

                <pb facs="0460" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg440"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Burlingame</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 72.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-09-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 14, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your despatch of the 18th of June, No. 83,
                    enclosing a copy of your communication of the 15th of the same month to the
                    Consul General Seward, containing your construction of the rights and duties of
                    American citizens in China, directions in relation to ships and passports, and
                    general suggestions in reference to the co-operative policy agreed upon by the
                    representatives of the treaty powers at Peking, has been received, and it is
                    approved with much commendation.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Anson Burlingame,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
